Z||000000||Wildcat||07-20-2001||01:40 AM||||My son's 86 Fiero has a weird intermittent problem.  Ocassionally it will not start, no spark.  Yet if they push start it, away it goes.  It is a 3.1 Lumina engine, but it did the same thing when it was a 2.8.  This happens hot or cold engine.  The part I can't figue is if they push start it, it goes, just won;t start using the starter, and it only happens about one day a week.<BR>Any ideas??||||reg||5
Z||000001||k2m4||07-20-2001||09:11 AM||||Does it turn over and not start? Does it not turn over? The car should tue\n over at the very minimum with all the ignition stuff not in line. I had a very similar problem with my 4 banger. turned out to be corroded terminals on the starter solenoid. It would intermittently not start and the problem was soooo infrequent that it was hard to pinpoint cause when everything was working it was working ok <P>good luck! any questions feel free to get a hold of me <P><P>------------------<BR>Kerm<BR>86 2M4<BR>86 1/2 GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||Wildcat||07-20-2001||07:36 PM||||Yup starter turns the engine over fine, just no spark, yet when pushed and clutch popped it starts okay, has spark then.||||reg||1
